@startuml duallity-config-ownership
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #34495E
  LifeLineBorderColor #34495E
  ParticipantBorderColor #34495E
}
title Configured WFST: borrowed input, owned grammar, one resource cache

participant "Caller buffers\n(options, operations, pairs)" as Caller #FFECB3
participant "duallity ABI\nvalidation + copy" as ABI #D6EAF8
participant "Dictionary\nquery-start snapshot" as Dict #D5F5E3
participant "duallity handle\nowned grammar + inspection" as Handle #D6EAF8
participant "lling-llang resource\nshared expansion cache" as Resource #FCF3CF

Caller -> ABI: configured constructor; borrowed pointers
activate ABI
ABI -> ABI: size/version/reserved checks\ncount, stride, UTF-8, grammar, limits
alt malformed or unsupported
  ABI --> Caller: typed failure; output null
else valid
  ABI -> ABI: deep-copy names and restrictions
  ABI -> Dict: capture exactly one revision
  Dict --> ABI: owned snapshot retain
  ABI -> Handle: install immutable grammar + snapshot
  ABI -> Resource: attach provider and sole cache policy
  Resource --> Handle: owned scalar-WFST resource
  ABI --> Caller: owned handle; input may be freed
end
deactivate ABI

Caller -> Handle: inspect effective options
Handle --> Caller: borrowed immutable view; valid until handle free
Caller -> Resource: retained resource clone, expansion, cache clear
Resource --> Caller: shared generation-safe payloads

legend bottom
  Amber: caller-owned storage, borrowed only during construction.
  Blue: duallity-owned validation, grammar, and handle.
  Green: immutable dictionary snapshot.
  Yellow: the single exported cache owner; resource clones share it.
end legend
@enduml
